      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 1. Delegation of Functions, Powers and Duties\nRespecting Street Activity Permits. Pursuant to subdivision f of section 8 of the New York City Charter, the Community Assistance Unit, acting through its Street Activity Permit Office, is delegated the authority to exercise all functions, powers and duties regarding the issuance of street activity permits and assessment of fees for street festivals, parties, celebrations, fairs and other events previously authorized to be performed by the Community Assistance Unit by Board of Estimate Resolution Cal. No. 47, dated July 17, 1980.",
